# Version Bumping

When bumping the NewsMinus version number, use the repo tool so all locations stay in sync:

```bash
python3 scripts/bump-version.py
```

Default bump is **minor** (same as Nunus). Agent edits use **patch** via **agent-patch-version**.

This updates:

1. **`manifest.json`** — `"version"`
2. **`safari/NewsMinusSafari.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj`** — `MARKETING_VERSION` and `CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION`
3. **`safari/scripts/gen_pbxproj.py`** — same version constants, then regenerates `project.pbxproj`

## Release levels

- **MAJOR** — newly supported site in `manifest.json`, or breaking changes
- **MINOR** — user-facing improvements within sites already shipped (`--minor` or **ship** when the user asks for a release bump)
- **PATCH** — bug fixes (default for agent edits; see **agent-patch-version**)

## Agent edits

When the agent changes committable files in a turn, bump **patch** per **agent-patch-version** (always-applied rule). Use `./scripts/bump-version.py --version X.Y.Z` after other edits.

Do not hand-edit version strings in only one file.
